-- src:62 | Administrative Arrangements Order:
-- src:63 | (a) means an instrument (a primary AAO) made by the Governor-General that is described as an Administrative Arrangements Order; and
-- src:64 | (b) includes an instrument made by the Governor-General that:
-- src:65 | (i) amends a primary AAO; or
-- src:66 | (ii) revokes a primary AAO and substitutes a new primary AAO.
-- src:67 | Note: The Administrative Arrangements Order sets out, from time to time, the matters dealt with by Departments of State of the Commonwealth together with the legislation administered by the Ministers for those Departments.
-- gloss: Administrative Arrangements Order stands for an instrument (a primary AAO) made by the Governor-General that is described as an Administrative Arrangements Order and covers the listed things
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "Administrative Arrangements Order" (src:62-67)
`section 2B defines Administrative Arrangements Order` MEANS
    `A meaning stated by the Act` OF `states a meaning and what is included`, JUST "an instrument (a primary AAO) made by the Governor-General that is described as an Administrative Arrangements Order", (LIST "amends a primary AAO", "revokes a primary AAO and substitutes a new primary AAO"), EMPTY, NOTHING, NOTHING

