-- src:366 | (4) In this section, coastal sea:
-- src:367 | (a) in relation to Australia, means:
-- src:368 | (i) the territorial sea of Australia; and
-- src:369 | (ii) the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea of Australia and not within the limits of a State or internal Territory;
-- src:370 | and includes the airspace over, and the sea-bed and subsoil beneath, any such sea; and
-- src:371 | (b) in relation to an external Territory, means:
-- src:372 | (i) the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory; and
-- src:373 | (ii) the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory and not within the limits of the Territory;
-- src:374 | and includes the airspace over, and the sea-bed and subsoil beneath, any such sea.
-- gloss: coastal sea stands for the first things listed and covers the listed things
-- members, pass 2: the airspace, sea-bed and subsoil limb is also listed as three phrases and three bare nouns; the two `and not within the limits of ...` limbs are one concept each and stay whole
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15B(4) "coastal sea" (src:366-374)
`section 15B(4) defines coastal sea` MEANS
    `A meaning stated by the Act` OF `states a meaning and what is included`, NOTHING, (LIST "the territorial sea of Australia", "the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea of Australia and not within the limits of a State or internal Territory", "the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory", "the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory and not within the limits of the Territory", "the airspace over, and the sea-bed and subsoil beneath, any such sea", "the airspace over any such sea", "the sea-bed beneath any such sea", "the subsoil beneath any such sea", "the airspace", "the sea-bed", "the subsoil"), EMPTY, NOTHING, NOTHING

