-- members, pass 2: the ten alternatives are also listed one at a time, bare and with their article
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(1) "person" (src:761)
`section 34C(1) defines person` MEANS
    `A meaning stated by the Act` OF `states what is included`, NOTHING, (LIST "a body corporate, office, commission, authority, committee, tribunal, board, institute, organization or other body however described", "body corporate", "a body corporate", "office", "an office", "commission", "a commission", "authority", "an authority", "committee", "a committee", "tribunal", "a tribunal", "board", "a board", "institute", "an institute", "organization", "an organization", "other body", "other body however described"), EMPTY, NOTHING, NOTHING

-- src:820 | holiday, in relation to the time for doing a thing, means:
-- src:821 | (a) a day that is a public holiday in the place in which the thing is to be or may be done; and
-- src:822 | (b) if the thing is to be or may be done at a particular office or other place—a day on which the place or office is closed for the whole day.
-- gloss: holiday stands for: a day that is a public holiday in the place in which the thing is to be or may be done; if the thing is to be or may be done at a particular office or other place—a day on which the place or office is closed for the whole day
-- members, pass 2: limbs (a) and (b) stay whole (the `or` joins verbs and places, not alternative members); the closure itself, after the dash, is also listed
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(3) "holiday" (src:820-822)
`section 36(3) defines holiday` MEANS
    `A meaning stated by the Act` OF `states a meaning`, NOTHING, (LIST "a day that is a public holiday in the place in which the thing is to be or may be done", "if the thing is to be or may be done at a particular office or other place—a day on which the place or office is closed for the whole day", "a day on which the place or office is closed for the whole day"), EMPTY, JUST "in relation to the time for doing a thing", NOTHING

